From 0a8bd532338a878fa3a9d3c901d07c6490f4b586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SovereignOS Build <build@sovereignos.local>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:34:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sovereignos: let a device-settings provider draw multi-toggle
 labels inside the buttons

Adds an opt-in boolean extra on ToggleInfo (TOGGLE_LABEL_IN_BUTTON), copies it into
ToggleModel.labelInsideButton, and lets SegmentedButtonPreference show the label as the
button text with the separate label row hidden. Absent or false keeps the stock rendering,
so other callers and older providers are unchanged. The approved AirPods settings design
shows the listening-mode text inside the buttons.

sovereignos: give a button that shows its own label room for the whole label

The default text-button padding of 24 dp on each side cut "Transparency" and "Noise cancel"
to "Transpare..." and "Noise can..." when three buttons share a row (seen on a Pixel 7a).
In labelInsideButton mode the horizontal padding is 8 dp. The stock icon-only rendering is
unchanged.

sovereignos: let a label inside a segmented button wrap to two lines

At font scale 1.3 "Transparency" was cut to "Transparen..." and at 2.0 to "Transp...", because
a button in labelInsideButton mode was single-line. It may now use two lines, hyphenate a word
that is wider than the button, and the buttons of the row take the height of the tallest one so
the row stays even. Stock icon-only rendering is unchanged.
